    Polish the AI combo suggestion card on Promotions
    
    Presentation only - aiSuggest(), the /combos/generate call and the aiNote
    contract are untouched, and all three fields (rationale, daypart, dropped) still
    render.
    
    The card was a flat grey box stacking four lines of identical 12px text, so the
    AI's reasoning, the daypart, the skipped-items warning and the editable hint all
    carried the same weight and none read as the point.
    
    Rebuilt in the house "AI speaks" vocabulary - the same warm gradient, soft
    orange orb and uppercase orange eyebrow as the Home briefing card - because this
    is the same act: the AI reporting something it worked out from the owner's data.
    Reusing that language rather than inventing a look for one card.
    
    Hierarchy now matches meaning:
      - eyebrow names the source ("Built from your last 30 days")
      - daypart moved out of prose into a chip with a clock glyph - it's a value,
        not a sentence, and it reads correctly for "All day" as well as "Lunch"
      - the rationale is the payload, so it gets the size and the room
      - skipped items become a proper amber callout, only when there are any
      - the editable hint drops to a quiet footer behind a hairline
    
